[37m**Pages:** About Me (hero, research threads, education timeline, projects, teaching, skills, contact) · Blog (index + 3 full articles with prev/next) · Publications (grouped by year, copy-BibTeX buttons) — plus RSS feed, sitemap, 404.[0m

[37m**Design:** warm-paper background with a deep-teal accent, serif headings / humanist sans body, hairline rules instead of box soup, numbered cards for research areas, a "journal-like" publication list. Accessibility built in (skip link, `aria-current`, heading order, AA contrast after tuning `--ink-mute`/`--gold`), dark mode with no flash, responsive to 320px, print stylesheet. **Zero dependencies and zero third-party requests** — the generator is stdlib-only Python, fonts are system fonts, so there is no npm, no CDN and nothing to exfiltrate.[0m

[37m## 3. The new deployment pipeline[0m

[37m`deploy.yml` now: `push` to `main` + `workflow_dispatch` → `permissions: {contents: read, pages: write, id-token: write}` → build → verify output + link check → `configure-pages` / `upload-pages-artifact` / `deploy-pages` (OIDC, no long-lived token, protected `github-pages` environment, `persist-credentials: false`, host-scoped concurrency). `build.yml` additionally greps workflows for a network tool followed by a URL, so a re-introduced exfiltration step **fails CI**.[0m

[37m**Verification run locally** (`./scripts/verify.sh`, which mirrors every workflow step): build ok (7 pages), link/self-containment check ok, no outbound calls, least-privilege ok; plus headless-browser checks — no horizontal overflow at 320/390/768/1024/1440, one `h1` per page, valid heading order, all `alt` present, theme toggle + persistence + BibTeX copy verified, zero console errors.[0m

